<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Krittibas Ojha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1400</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Krittivas Ojha, Krittivasa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Krittibas Ojha was a Bengali poet who wrote the Krittivasi Ramayan, a free retelling of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramayana">Ramayana</a> in Bengali verse, probably in the early fifteenth century. Written in simple language and adding episodes from Bengali devotion, it became the most popular version of the epic in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, recited and read in households for centuries, and helped establish Bengali as a literary language.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/krittibas-ojha.jpg" alt="Krittibas Ojha" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mukherjiavijit · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krittibas_Memorial_ver1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Its court patronised literature in Bengali as well as Persian: Maladhar Basu composed the Sri Krishna Vijaya under Rukunuddin Barbak Shah, <b>Krittibas Ojha</b> produced the most popular Bengali Ramayana in this era, and the governor of Chittagong under Husain Shah sponsored a Bengali rendering of the Mahabharata.</blockquote><a href="/empire/bengal-sultanate">Bengal Sultanate · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Phulia, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=23.24,88.5&amp;year=1400" aria-label="Phulia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6912 1306 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Krittibas Ojha"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7362 1576h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7362 1576h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=23.24,88.5&amp;year=1400">What was here in 1400? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
